{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 875 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "70f58c7cf34a2a409119e733dc4793dcefed32a89d87f723b62418796738b707" :edb/db-before-t 874 :edb/db-after-t 875 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534187 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:32:34.006Z" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162113 1038 #edb/ref 17592186413415 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162392 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159554 13194139534187 17592186045417 false] [17592186162392 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413413 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162392 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162392 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}24xy, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}).$" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162392 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$f(x, y) = {24xy,\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < 1, 0 < y < 1 - x \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind $P(Y < X \\mid X = \\frac{1}{3})$." 13194139534187 17592186045417 false] [17592186162392 1074 "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1-x}24xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1-x} \\\\  & =12x(1-x)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =12x(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)={\\begin{aligned}12x(x-1)^{2}, & \\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x<1,0<y<1-x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24xy}{12x(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) & =P(Y<\\frac{1}{3}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2y}{{(\\frac{1}{3}-1)}^{2}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\frac{1}{18}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162396 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159578 13194139534187 17592186045417 false] [17592186162396 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413412 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162396 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162396 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186162396 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n$f(x, y) = {(2y(2x + 3y))/(5),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid y)$ for $1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 1$." 13194139534187 17592186045417 false] [17592186162396 1074 "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{4xy}{5}+\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{5}+\\frac{6x{y}^{2}}{5}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8y}{5}+\\frac{12{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{2y}{5}-\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{6y}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5})}{(\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413416 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413417 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413418 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1045 "Conditional Distributions for Continuous Random Variables" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1046 #edb/ref 17592186413418 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050535 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413396 1053 #uuid "8d71dbb8-3f6b-51a3-b4b2-a5b2c8b23a9b" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413397 1080 "\\frac{15}{16}" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413397 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413397 1083 #uuid "0232ff5b-0d05-5778-88a0-ff0af66fc111" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413398 1080 "\\frac{27}{64}" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413398 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413398 1083 #uuid "0d7ebaa8-7f99-5427-8a2f-237d9f6e4410" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413399 1080 "\\frac{8}{9}" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413399 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413399 1083 #uuid "291ffaa1-af34-572c-8208-632d599387b4" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413400 1080 "\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}" 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413400 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534187 17592186045417 true] [17592186413400 1083 #uuid "2b4b973f